Repository Bio / Short Description (For GitHub Sidebar)
A comprehensive Hospital Management System built with Flask, SQLite, and Bootstrap 5, featuring secure role-based portals for Admins, Doctors, and Patients.

🏥 Hospital Management System (HMS)
A robust, web-based Hospital Management System designed to streamline hospital operations, patient appointment scheduling, and medical history tracking. Developed as part of the Modern Application Development (MAD 1) curriculum.

✨ Key Features
🔧 Admin Portal
Dashboard Metrics: Real-time overview of total doctors, registered patients, and scheduled appointments.

Staff Management: Full CRUD operations to manage doctor profiles, departments, and availability.

System Monitoring: View and manage all system appointments and user accounts with search and filtering capabilities.

🩺 Doctor Portal
Schedule Management: View daily and weekly assigned appointments and patient lists.

Availability Tracking: Easily update 7-day availability slots.

Treatment Logging: Record diagnoses, prescriptions, and treatment notes directly against completed appointments.

🧑‍⚕️ Patient Portal
Self-Service Registration: Secure sign-up and profile management.

Doctor Discovery: Search for doctors by department, specialization, and real-time 7-day availability.

Appointment Booking: Seamless booking, rescheduling, and cancellation with built-in validation preventing double-booking conflicts.

Medical History: Comprehensive view of past appointments, prescriptions, and diagnosis reports.

🛠️ Tech Stack
Backend: Python, Flask, Flask-SQLAlchemy, Flask-Login

Frontend: Jinja2 Templates, HTML5, CSS, Bootstrap 5

Database: SQLite (Programmatically initialized via SQLAlchemy)
  📁 Project Structure
Plaintext
hospital_project/
│
├── app.py                 # Main entry point & application setup
├── models.py              # SQLAlchemy database models & schemas
├── routes.py              # Controller logic and route endpoints
├── instance/              
│   └── database.sqlite    # SQLite database (auto-generated)
├── static/                
│   └── css/
│       └── style.css      # Custom styling sheets
└── templates/             
    ├── base.html          # Global layout template
    ├── login.html         # User authentication view
    ├── admin/             # Admin dashboard & management views
    ├── doctor/            # Doctor portal & schedule views
    └── patient/           # Patient dashboard & booking views
🚀 Getting Started Locally
Follow these instructions to get a copy of the project up and running on your local machine for development and testing.

Prerequisites
Python 3.8+ installed on your machine.

pip package manager.

Installation Steps
Clone the repository:

Bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/hospital-management-system.git
cd hospital-management-system
Create and activate a virtual environment:

Bash
python -m venv venv
# On Windows:
venv\Scripts\activate
# On macOS/Linux:
source venv/bin/activate
Install dependencies:

Bash
pip install flask flask-sqlalchemy flask-login
Initialize and run the application:

Bash
python app.py
Access the application:
Open your web browser and navigate to [http://127.0.0.1:5000](http://127.0.0.1:5000)
